# No Demo / Dummy Data

This project must use **real APIs and real data only**.

## Required

- Call Open Prices (pre-prod: `prices.openfoodfacts.net`) and Open Food Facts APIs for live data
- Persist only what the user or those APIs actually produced (receipts, validated barcodes, consent, tokens)
- Show empty / loading / error / "unknown" states when data is missing — never invent substitutes

## Forbidden

- Hardcoded sample receipts, products, barcodes, scores, stores, or history
- Mock / fake / stub API responses used as the default path in the app
- Seed files, fixtures, or "demo mode" that populate UI with fake content
- Placeholder objects presented as real results (e.g. Nutri-Score `"b"` with no OFF fetch)

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — fake receipt for UI
const demoReceipt = {
  storeName: "Demo Market",
  items: [{ displayName: "Milk", barcode: "123", product: { nutriScoreGrade: "a" } }]
}

// ✅ GOOD — empty until APIs return data
const items = []
// after Open Prices extract + OFF enrich:
// items come from API responses only
```

## Exceptions

- TypeScript types / empty defaults (`null`, `[]`, `unknown`) are fine
- Cypress E2E may intercept network **only inside tests** — never ship mock data in app runtime
- Isolation fixture `src/data/mockReceipt.js` for `/review` and `/score` when the session is empty or `?mock=1`, so Review/Score can work before Capture writes API items. Do not treat it as live Open Prices data.
